responsibly<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#tour\">Our guided tour of Albufera des Grau<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#faqs\">Frequently Asked Questions<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#fuentes\">Sources and useful links<\/a><\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n  <\/nav>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"que-es\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>What is a Biosphere Reserve?<\/h2>\n    <p>UNESCO Biosphere Reserves are learning sites for sustainable development: territories where human life is reconciled with the conservation of nature and culture. More info on the official website of <a href=\"https:\/\/www.unesco.org\/en\/mab\/wnbr\/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UNESCO \u00b7 MAB Programme<\/a>. <\/p>\n\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/30269260\/pexels-photo-30269260.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Footbridge over Mediterranean wetland for environmental education in Menorca\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"por-que-menorca\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>Why Menorca is one (since 1993)<\/h2>\n    <p>Menorca was declared a <strong>Biosphere Reserve on October 7, 1993<\/strong>. See the official file at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.unesco.org\/en\/mab\/menorca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UNESCO \u00b7 Menorca<\/a> and the portal of the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.menorcabiosfera.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Consell Insular de Menorca<\/a>. In <strong>2019<\/strong>, the scope was extended to the entire marine environment (up to 12 nautical miles), reaching <strong>514,485 ha<\/strong>. Informative summary: <a href=\"https:\/\/menorcapreservation.org\/protect-our-marine-environments\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Menorca Preservation<\/a>.   <\/p>\n\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/27404114\/pexels-photo-27404114.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Menorca coast with cliffs and turquoise sea, Biosphere Reserve\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"zonificacion\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>Zoning: core, buffer, and transition<\/h2>\n    <p>Management is organized into three zones: <strong>core<\/strong> (strict protection), <strong>buffer<\/strong> (compatible activities), and <strong>transition<\/strong> (daily life and sustainable economy). Full definition at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.unesco.org\/en\/mab\/wnbr\/about\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UNESCO \u00b7 What are the Reserves?<\/a>. <\/p>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"albufera\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>Albufera des Grau: heart of the wetland<\/h2>\n    <p>The <strong>Parc Natural de s\u2019Albufera des Grau<\/strong> includes a lagoon, dunes, wild olive forests, coastline, and islets. It is the largest wetland area in Menorca and the <em>core zone<\/em> of the Reserve. Official info: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.caib.es\/sites\/espaisnaturalsprotegits\/es\/parc_natural_de_salbufera_des_grau\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Govern Illes Balears \u00b7 Parc Natural<\/a>. The <strong>Centre Rodr\u00edguez Femen\u00edas<\/strong> offers maps, binoculars to borrow, and suggestions: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.illesbalears.travel\/en\/menorca\/nature-park-albufera-des-grau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Illes Balears \u00b7 Albufera des Grau<\/a>.   <\/p>\n\n    <p><strong>Signposted itineraries<\/strong> (easy level): <a href=\"https:\/\/www.caib.es\/sites\/espaisnaturalsprotegits\/es\/parc_natural_de_salbufera_des_grau\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Mirador de Cala Llimpa, Santa Madrona and Sa Gola<\/a>. PDF map: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.caib.es\/sites\/espaisnaturalsprotegits\/f\/487585\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Itineraries \u00b7 PDF<\/a>. <\/p>\n\n    <p>The park is part of <strong>Natura 2000<\/strong> (SCI\/SPA <strong>ES0000234<\/strong>): file at <a href=\"https:\/\/www.miteco.gob.es\/es\/biodiversidad\/temas\/espacios-protegidos\/red-natura-2000\/lic_baleares.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">MITECO<\/a> and informative brochure <a href=\"https:\/\/www.miteco.gob.es\/content\/dam\/miteco\/es\/biodiversidad\/temas\/conservacion-de-la-biodiversidad\/folletoespaciosnatura2000_costaestemenorca_castellano_tcm30-542231.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Natura 2000 East Coast (PDF)<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/19759540\/pexels-photo-19759540.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Sa Gola footbridge over the Albufera des Grau wetland\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/20758527\/pexels-photo-20758527.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Water bird flying over a Mediterranean wetland in Menorca\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"visita-responsable\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>How to visit responsibly (10 keys)<\/h2>\n    <ol>\n      <li><strong>Stay on authorized trails<\/strong> (Cala Llimpa, Santa Madrona and Sa Gola).<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Observe wildlife silently<\/strong> and from a distance; do not approach nests or hiding places.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Zero waste:<\/strong> everything that comes in, goes out with you; avoid single-use plastics.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Respect posidonia and dunes:<\/strong> do not step on or uproot vegetation; do not move driftwood.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Water and sun:<\/strong> bring a water bottle and protection; avoid peak sun hours in summer.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>No collecting of species<\/strong> (plants, shells, fossils).<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Dogs<\/strong> always on a leash and away from sensitive bird areas.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>No drones<\/strong> in sensitive areas or without specific permits.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Local economy:<\/strong> prioritize crafts, km0 products, and responsible services.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Responsible transport:<\/strong> share a car, use bus or bike when possible.<\/li>\n    <\/ol>\n\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/5243546\/pexels-photo-5243546.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Mediterranean dunes with vegetation and sea in Menorca\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"tour\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>Guided tour of Albufera des Grau (2 h \u00b7 easy level)<\/h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Meeting point:<\/strong> Rodr\u00edguez Femen\u00edas Reception\/Interpretation Center (Ma\u00f3\u2013Es Grau, km 3.5).<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Proposed route:<\/strong> combination of <em>Mirador de Cala Llimpa<\/em> (1.7 km) + <em>Santa Madrona<\/em> (section) depending on the season and weather.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Key topics:<\/strong> Menorca and UNESCO, zoning, Mediterranean wetlands and birds, management of <em>sa Gola<\/em>, seasonal change of the landscape.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Accessibility:<\/strong> adapted options in <em>sa Gola<\/em> (check availability at the center).<\/li>\n      <li><strong>What to bring:<\/strong> comfortable shoes, hat, water, binoculars if you have them.<\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:8px\">Are you interested in other routes? Check out our <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">list of excursions in Menorca<\/a>, the <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/guided-tour-of-ciutadella\/\">guided tour of Ciutadella<\/a>, and the <a href=\"\/visita-guiada-por-mahon\/\">guided tour of Mah\u00f3n<\/a>. <\/p>\n    <div class=\"vm-cta\">\n      <a href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" class=\"vm-btn vm-btn-whatsapp\">\ud83d\udcf2 Check schedules and book<\/a>\n      <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\" class=\"vm-btn\">\ud83c\udf3f See all excursions<\/a>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"vm-section vm-faq\">\n    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\n    <div class=\"vm-faq-item\">\n      <h3>When is the best time to go?<\/h3>\n      <p>All year round. In autumn and spring there is a greater passage of birds; in summer we recommend the first hours of the day. <\/p>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"vm-faq-item\">\n      <h3>Is it suitable for families?<\/h3>\n      <p>Yes, the official itineraries are easy and well signposted.<\/p>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"vm-faq-item\">\n      <h3>Is it possible to get there without a car?<\/h3>\n      <p>In season there are bus\/taxi combinations to Es Grau. If you need it, we coordinate the logistics. <\/p>\n    <\/div>\n    <div class=\"vm-faq-item\">\n      <h3>Can I use a drone?<\/h3>\n      <p>Not in sensitive wildlife areas or without permits. Ask us first to avoid penalties. <\/p>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/section>\n\n  <section id=\"fuentes\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>Sources and useful links<\/h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.unesco.org\/en\/mab\/menorca\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UNESCO \u00b7 Menorca (official file)<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.menorcabiosfera.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Consell Insular \u00b7 Menorca Biosphere<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/menorcapreservation.org\/protect-our-marine-environments\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Menorca Preservation (2019 marine extension)<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.caib.es\/sites\/espaisnaturalsprotegits\/es\/parc_natural_de_salbufera_des_grau\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Parc Natural de s\u2019Albufera des Grau (info and itineraries)<\/a> \u00b7 <a href=\"https:\/\/www.caib.es\/sites\/espaisnaturalsprotegits\/f\/487585\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PDF Map<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.illesbalears.travel\/en\/menorca\/nature-park-albufera-des-grau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Rodr\u00edguez Femen\u00edas Center<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"https:\/\/www.miteco.gob.es\/es\/biodiversidad\/temas\/espacios-protegidos\/red-natura-2000\/lic_baleares.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Natura 2000 \u00b7 SCI\/SPA ES0000234<\/a><\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <div class=\"vm-sticky-cta\">\n    <a href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" class=\"vm-btn vm-btn-whatsapp\">\ud83d\udcf2 Book via WhatsApp<\/a>\n  <\/div>\n\n\n<\/div>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Menorca has been a Biosphere Reserve since 1993. We offer a guided tour of Albufera des Grau to discover its wetland, birds, and easy trails, with tips for visiting responsibly. Book via WhatsApp at +34 649 902 301.  <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":2,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[73,72,117,116],"tags":[118,119,122,125,124,123,120,121],"class_list":["post-1078","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-beaches-of-menorca","category-discover-menorca","category-guides-and-routes","category-menorca-biosphere-reserve","tag-albufera-des-grau","tag-biosphere-reserve","tag-birds","tag-ea